#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161771 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "c68d70a2-e4f8-5f08-8220-3df420a1e199" :question/math-academy-id "e-8156" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n![](images/49/494cd45f9c85aaa8703ed4c5a0cac805b69cd91bbef979a2c3ff1ffac1592763.png)" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA = A^T\n$$\n\nEquivalently, $a_{ij} = a_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P=P^T.$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q=Q^T.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since $r_{12} \\neq r_{21},$ we obtain $R \\neq R^T.$\n![](images/4d/4db4bdfa8aaeac26238404107f195847eaccde9e595a7d1a0678053e2b149d0e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161816 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "b159d52a-a436-5743-9151-2e147364a41d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8478" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A$ is *any* $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A+A^T$ is always symmetric.\n\n- The difference between two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is symmetric.\n\n- The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA = A^T\n$$\n\nEquivalently, $a_{ij} = a_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+{A}^{T})^{T} & ={A}^{T}+({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}+A \\\\  & =A+{A}^{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the sum or difference between two symmetric matrices is symmetric.\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n![](images/ca/ca86224294fba346835dab8fcfd7a045dfe1bda723499dceca4b60339ece6300.png)\nTheir product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa99686-720d-5c83-8792-909de2767703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the matrices are symmetric" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425148} {:answer/id #uuid "13edd389-e8cd-52c8-8f6e-2c34ed7ad05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425149} {:answer/id #uuid "33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425150} {:answer/id #uuid "655424c1-b811-5aaf-8538-b1da76023605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425151} {:answer/id #uuid "65dc2a15-12f3-5c0d-999e-1bc8c09548b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425150} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dcd0455-6677-5df3-b08a-01a2a95723e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea940e2f-7cf1-5b69-9241-9cde37e5f341" :question/math-academy-id "q-140503" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${p}_{12}\\ne {p}_{21},$ we obtain $P\\ne {P}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b67bf2d-f434-5cbf-a65f-fe92576ed3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469638} {:answer/id #uuid "1f304f6a-e85b-5ca9-8056-745663c7ef23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b67bf2d-f434-5cbf-a65f-fe92576ed3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469638} :answer-field/id #uuid "04035bc7-0baa-52a2-8819-5785c4397711" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a25bb71a-4230-5f5d-aaf6-2df76c7f39c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469640} {:answer/id #uuid "82cc5f65-1d57-56f6-b5fe-cc38b670cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82cc5f65-1d57-56f6-b5fe-cc38b670cf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469641} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c0a8bf-9374-501d-9297-e531eb25d3f0" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "689daa18-2b9c-5f89-9c4a-2575e6717d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469642} {:answer/id #uuid "2223f70f-5ec1-579a-a3a0-521b192241b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "689daa18-2b9c-5f89-9c4a-2575e6717d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469642} :answer-field/id #uuid "800cf770-f16d-5241-92e2-0bfe2665859c" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "225f8bdf-5da4-5137-973e-d6466e5f7f7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93985" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${p}_{12}\\ne {p}_{21},$ we obtain $P\\ne {P}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc0be98-e287-58d8-8b2c-e57d0709ae44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448822} {:answer/id #uuid "d4948f79-c7c8-5639-819a-cd61729a3714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4948f79-c7c8-5639-819a-cd61729a3714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448823} :answer-field/id #uuid "5550f4ed-86c5-5c97-864d-aa737d189eeb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "733dd422-332d-5ac1-bd98-df4c965e888d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448824} {:answer/id #uuid "7af5d31f-43de-53e3-b3f8-80b2d1a9c9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7af5d31f-43de-53e3-b3f8-80b2d1a9c9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448825} :answer-field/id #uuid "b59b6c28-d8c2-5120-bb8c-d706a0e786fd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89550eca-a604-5392-90ab-129c47480727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448826} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed9e463-582b-5949-bc8c-6e012d4e7b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89550eca-a604-5392-90ab-129c47480727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448826} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a624701-1d1e-5fa7-ad82-6549f6ebba57" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8be226ee-498f-567c-82d1-206ed205336b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96046" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A$ is *any* matrix, then $A{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric.\n- **II.** The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- **III.** The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A{A}^{T})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{T}{A}^{T} \\\\  & =A{A}^{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61f9b779-a82b-5fca-ac7c-8326f052042f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452263} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a19fce-bfec-59e9-b174-01dd728ea53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61f9b779-a82b-5fca-ac7c-8326f052042f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452263} :answer-field/id #uuid "027ffc36-9391-569a-9d2f-da2a80b366dc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0b1bee2-eead-5899-9436-3a5e41c5d534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452265} {:answer/id #uuid "5c95db47-f37c-5361-aca9-caa8ca8ccc7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0b1bee2-eead-5899-9436-3a5e41c5d534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452265} :answer-field/id #uuid "3698aa5e-23d2-5ab3-84e9-157fdeec0f61" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b91e26b4-0173-5667-9919-d76bd3bc5172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452267} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9e1009-c7de-59b4-8f5d-83345258f1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d9e1009-c7de-59b4-8f5d-83345258f1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452268} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cfe9278-620c-5f30-9b43-3e38a539af4d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6c182c5-819c-5206-a031-9309a3557f8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96589" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{2}$ is always symmetric.\n\n- **II.** The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n\n- **III.** If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{2}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed889475-ee9c-533a-8ed7-519387cf84ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452275} {:answer/id #uuid "62ca60ad-f94f-54fa-a2aa-9d8d07b4e4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ca60ad-f94f-54fa-a2aa-9d8d07b4e4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452276} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3d3a26b-faad-53a5-854d-c0ce0d455ccd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452985} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecf353d3-2d53-5e63-8b1b-661cb9cb2eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452277} {:answer/id #uuid "909b121b-5859-5703-a1e4-479d1c1bdd03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecf353d3-2d53-5e63-8b1b-661cb9cb2eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452277} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c88bb5-4a8e-5849-bf4a-edd46eb5f6a3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "570d980e-c237-5c27-a69f-2dee15bb061a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452279} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4665db-639e-5f41-9895-fb286356fc79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e4665db-639e-5f41-9895-fb286356fc79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452280} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c01aa01-2f35-5253-9a12-c161f9fc3268" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "df6e5142-313f-5de3-a45d-4da4b737f0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-96594" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric.\n- **II.** If $A$ is *any* $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists).\n- **III.** If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the non-singular matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{-1}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{T}A)^{T} & ={A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb469e2b-45b7-5c77-8add-fd24d81f76d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477503} {:answer/id #uuid "66140b4b-4324-5e27-a1dd-7c616d17027a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb469e2b-45b7-5c77-8add-fd24d81f76d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477503} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbadfff9-d053-5773-a9d3-3a35eae8db62" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb71d94b-854a-5f6f-ab43-827916efb668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477505} {:answer/id #uuid "14acc8e7-2f06-5015-818b-6576056fa2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14acc8e7-2f06-5015-818b-6576056fa2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477506} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c0a27b-9b21-5183-a539-76f7d460db30" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1040037-a9ef-55ea-854b-01e535caaedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477507} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b8f46f-b9ea-5dc8-9bb6-bb0919a4a4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b8f46f-b9ea-5dc8-9bb6-bb0919a4a4d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477508} :answer-field/id #uuid "2734b571-73f6-5d0e-a051-dd621c984e1d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2943df26-2edc-5f92-bec7-1493042a2419" :question/math-academy-id "q-96595" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$  matrix, then $A-{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric.\n- **II.** The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- **III.** If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists).\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, $A-{A}^{T}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{A}^{T} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
